👉 Enum is a special class for creating named constants.
👉 It is imported using from enum import Enum.
👉 Each enum member has a .name and a .value.
👉 Enums make code cleaner, safer, and easier to maintain.
👉 They are ideal for fixed values like roles, statuses, colors, days, and months.

👉 Integer Enum => An Integer Enum is an enumeration where each member is assigned an integer value.

    from enum import Enum
    class Status(Enum):
        PENDING = 1
        APPROVED = 2
        REJECTED = 3
    print(Status.APPROVED)
    print(Status.APPROVED.name)
    print(Status.APPROVED.value)
---------------------------------------------
  from enum import Enum
  class StudentStatus(Enum):
      ACTIVE = 1
      INACTIVE = 2
      SUSPENDED = 3
  student = StudentStatus.ACTIVE
  print(student)

👉 String Enum => A String Enum stores string values instead of integers.

    from enum import Enum
    class Gender(Enum):
        MALE = "Male"
        FEMALE = "Female"
        OTHER = "Other"
    print(Gender.MALE)
    print(Gender.MALE.value)

👉 Mixed Values

    from enum import Enum
    class Demo(Enum):
        A = 1
        B = "Hello"
        C = 3.14
    print(Demo.B.value)

👉 Using auto() => The auto() function automatically assigns values to Enum members.

    from enum import Enum, auto
    class Color(Enum):
        RED = auto()
        GREEN = auto()
        BLUE = auto()
    print(Color.RED.value)
    print(Color.GREEN.value)
    print(Color.BLUE.value)

👉 Prevent Duplicate Values (@unique) => The @unique decorator ensures that all Enum values are unique. 
                                          If duplicate values exist, Python raises a ValueError.

    from enum import Enum, unique
    @unique
    class Fruit(Enum):
        APPLE = 1
        MANGO = 2
        ORANGE = 2
    print(Fruit.ORANGE)

Summary
  👉 Integer Enums store integer values.
  👉 String Enums store string values.
  👉 auto() automatically generates sequential values.
  👉 Duplicate values create aliases by default.
  👉 @unique prevents duplicate values.
  👉 Prefer keeping all Enum values of the same data type for clean and maintainable code.

